## How the service works
<!-- Describe the end-to-end flow in your own words: what happens from HTTP request to stored result -->

- A Student submits an answer set from the "frontend", and the client sends a POST call to the server. `/assessments/{assessmentId}/submit` containing a body of raw JSON, with student ID and question answers. 
- .NET maps the URL to the endpoint
- Maps to the submit function call, which injects the service and database
- Controller asks databse if the assessment ID exists, and saves the submission, returning the submission as 200 OK. 

so,. http request -> conntroller -> service & database

## Scoring function
<!-- How did you approach implementing calculate_score? Any edge cases that gave you pause? -->
- I chose to use a nested for loop to iterate through the assessment sections and corresponding questions. Tallying score, overall percentage, and section grade iteratively like you might in real life when 
grading a test. 
- There are certain edge cases not included in the tests that i did consider: 
  - What if there is no answer included for a question
  - What if a section contains no questions? 

